  "notes": "Lebanon County Republicans elect county committee members in presidential-year primaries (the 2026 primary had a Democratic county committee contest but no Republican one). Each of the 60 precincts elects 3 members (MEMBER OF REPUBLICAN COUNTY COMMITTEE, vote for 3), so seats are labelled Member 1-3. filled = one of the top-3 ballot candidates who received votes. unknown = a seat with no ballot candidate where write-in votes were cast; this includes seats a named write-in may have won, which stay unknown. empty = no ballot candidate and no write-in votes. Lebanon 5th Ward East had a tie between two ballot candidates for the third seat; the county's tie-breaker sheet records it was settled by drawing lots, so that seat is counted filled. Other entries on that sheet are write-in ties and were not used. Appointments and vacancies since April 2024 are not captured."
